# AIM Studio — Public Page Performance Audit & Optimization Plan

## Summary

After reading every relevant file, here is the full picture of what is causing slowness on public pages for 4G users, and the exact changes proposed.

**No redesign. No schema changes. No db:push. No new packages. Admin panel is untouched.**

---

## Findings

### What is already good
- `globals.css` already disables `backdrop-filter` on mobile, kills the SVG noise on mobile, disables canvas `Scene3D` on mobile/reduced-motion
- `next.config.ts` already strips heavy binaries from the deployment bundle
- `HeroBackground` already batches 3 separate API calls into 1 (`/api/admin/media?page=X`)
- `WorksPageClient` already code-splits `SearchBar`, `RollRow`, `HoverPreviewCard` with `dynamic()`
- `[locale]/layout.tsx` already removed `force-dynamic` so ISR works
- Next.js image optimizer is re-enabled with AVIF/WebP and proper `deviceSizes`
- Google Fonts are self-hosted via `next/font/google` with `display: 'swap'`

### Root causes of remaining slowness

| # | Issue | Impact | File |
|---|-------|--------|------|
| 1 | `/api/site-settings` has **no Cache-Control header** — fetched by `SiteSettingsContext` on every page load, every user | 1 DB hit per visitor (100ms+ cold) | `src/app/api/site-settings/route.ts` |
| 2 | `SiteSettingsContext` calls `fetchSettings()` immediately on mount but **also re-fetches** on every `storage` event — no dedup | Minor JS churn | `src/context/SiteSettingsContext.tsx` |
| 3 | `HeroBackground` fires `fetch('/api/admin/media?page=...')` **without** `Cache-Control` on the client, and the API itself **only sets `s-maxage`** (CDN cache) but not `max-age` (browser cache) — every hard reload re-fetches from the server | ~200-400ms on 4G | `src/app/api/admin/media/route.ts` |
| 4 | `WatchPlayer.tsx` is **2 057 lines / 118 KB** and is `import`ed statically in `ProjectDetailClient2.tsx` (line 10). It gets bundled into the project-detail page chunk even for users who never click the trailer. | +90–120 kB gzipped chunk on mobile | `src/components/ProjectDetailClient2.tsx` |
| 5 | `ScrollReveal3D` sets `willChange: 'opacity, transform'` on **every desktop project card** — this promotes every card to a GPU layer at parse time, consuming VRAM even before the user scrolls | Jank on low-RAM phones | `src/components/ScrollReveal3D.tsx` |
| 6 | `WorksPageClient.tsx` imports `Scene3D` **statically** (line 6) — it is only rendered on desktop but the code is in every bundle | ~10 KB wasted on mobile | `src/components/WorksPageClient.tsx` |
| 7 | `globals.css` is **156 KB** — it is already well-structured but is served as a single file. It contains admin-specific styles (`.admin-*`) that are included on every public page. | ~30–40 KB CSS payload that could be split | `src/app/globals.css` |
| 8 | `SponsorBannerSection.tsx` uses inline `<style>` for the shimmer keyframe on every render — minor but repeated DOM write | Negligible | `src/components/SponsorBannerSection.tsx` |

---

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Add browser Cache-Control to `/api/site-settings`

#### [MODIFY] [route.ts](file:///c:/Users/mxz/Desktop/my%20website/aim-platform/src/app/api/site-settings/route.ts)

Add `Cache-Control: public, s-maxage=60, stale-while-revalidate=300` so the CDN caches it for 1 minute and browsers can use a stale copy for up to 5 minutes. The admin panel calls `clearSiteSettingsCache()` and `refresh()` after saving, so stale data will never persist after an admin update.

---

### 2. Add `max-age` (browser cache) to `/api/admin/media`

#### [MODIFY] [route.ts](file:///c:/Users/mxz/Desktop/my%20website/aim-platform/src/app/api/admin/media/route.ts)

Currently has `s-maxage=300, stale-while-revalidate=3600` (CDN-only). Add `max-age=60` so the browser can serve from its own cache for 60 seconds on soft navigations. The admin media manager already calls `revalidatePath` after uploads, so fresh data is never blocked.

---

### 3. Lazy-load `WatchPlayer` in `ProjectDetailClient2.tsx`

#### [MODIFY] [ProjectDetailClient2.tsx](file:///c:/Users/mxz/Desktop/my%20website/aim-platform/src/components/ProjectDetailClient2.tsx)

Replace the static import on line 10:
```diff
-import WatchPlayer from '@/components/WatchPlayer'
+import dynamic from 'next/dynamic'
+const WatchPlayer = dynamic(() => import('@/components/WatchPlayer'), { ssr: false })
```

`WatchPlayer` is never shown until the user clicks "Watch Trailer" (which calls `setIsTrailerVisible(true)` and then scrolls to the trailer section). It is also only rendered when `project.trailerUrl` is truthy. Lazy-loading removes ~90–120 kB from the initial page-load chunk for project detail pages on mobile.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> `WatchPlayer` is used in two places: `ProjectDetailClient2.tsx` (public, for trailers) and the dedicated `/watch` page. Only the `ProjectDetailClient2` import needs to be dynamic. The `/watch` page already renders `WatchPlayer` eagerly by design.

---

### 4. Remove `willChange` from `ScrollReveal3D` until intersection

#### [MODIFY] [ScrollReveal3D.tsx](file:///c:/Users/mxz/Desktop/my%20website/aim-platform/src/components/ScrollReveal3D.tsx)

`willChange: 'opacity, transform'` forces the browser to allocate a GPU compositing layer **immediately** for every card, before the user even scrolls. This is counterproductive on mobile. The fix: only set `willChange` at the moment of transition start, and clear it afterward.

Change the inline style to:
```diff
- willChange: 'opacity, transform',
```
And add to the observer callback:
```js
el.style.willChange = 'opacity, transform'
setTimeout(() => {
    el.style.opacity = '1'
    el.style.transform = 'none'
    setTimeout(() => { el.style.willChange = 'auto' }, 900) // clear after animation ends
}, delay)
```

---

### 5. Code-split `Scene3D` in `WorksPageClient`

#### [MODIFY] [WorksPageClient.tsx](file:///c:/Users/mxz/Desktop/my%20website/aim-platform/src/components/WorksPageClient.tsx)

`Scene3D` is already guarded inside `Scene3D.tsx` (returns nothing on mobile). But the import on line 6 is static — the module code ships to mobile. Convert to dynamic:

```diff
-import Scene3D from '@/components/Scene3D'
+import dynamic from 'next/dynamic'
+const Scene3D = dynamic(() => import('@/components/Scene3D'), { ssr: false, loading: () => null })
```

`Scene3DClient.tsx` already does this for the homepage; `WorksPageClient` was missed.

---

### 6. Move shimmer keyframe from inline `<style>` to `globals.css`

#### [MODIFY] [SponsorBannerSection.tsx](file:///c:/Users/mxz/Desktop/my%20website/aim-platform/src/components/SponsorBannerSection.tsx) + [globals.css](file:///c:/Users/mxz/Desktop/my%20website/aim-platform/src/app/globals.css)

The `@keyframes sponsorShimmer` is injected inline every render. Move it to `globals.css` (already has a `@keyframes shimmer`). Minor but eliminates repeated style-injection on every mount.

