## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q1: Can we add `max-age=60` to the site-settings API response?**
> This means browsers will not re-check the API for 60 seconds. For admin users updating settings, this is fine because the admin panel clears `localStorage` and forces a re-fetch. But if a non-admin user's browser has cached the old settings for up to 60 seconds, they may see a stale navbar briefly. Is 60 seconds acceptable, or would you prefer `no-store` for logged-in users and `public` only for anonymous?

> [!NOTE]
> **Q2: CSS splitting** — `globals.css` is 156 KB and contains both public and admin styles. We could split it into `globals.css` (public, ~80 KB) and `admin.css` (admin-only, ~76 KB) and import `admin.css` only in the `/admin` layout. This is the highest-effort change and carries the most risk of breaking admin UI. Want to include it in this pass, or defer?

